<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Berones</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 133 BCE (approx.) · capital Vareia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Celtic people of the upper Ebro in La Rioja, whose towns Vareia, Tritium and Libia lay on the routes into the Meseta.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Berones lived in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-rioja-spain">La Rioja</a>, from about the 4th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> described them as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a>, and their neighbours were the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/autrigones">Autrigones</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pellendones">Pellendones</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vascones">Vascones</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their government. Their towns included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vareia">Vareia</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/logrono">Logroño</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tritium-magallum">Tritium</a> and Libia, and they lived from farming the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley and herding. They reportedly served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> in conflicts of the 2nd century BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They came under Roman control in the 2nd century BCE during the Celtiberian wars. In 76 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-sertorius">Sertorius</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vareia">Vareia</a> during his war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The Berones were absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tritium-magallum">Tritium Magallum</a> became a major Roman pottery centre.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 133 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:5.31%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 133 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vareia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Spain</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Beronians</dd></dl></aside></div>
